 recent polls, while prediction markets give him roughly a three-in-four chance of winning. De La Cruz retains the incumbency advantage and a larger war chest, keeping this genuinely competitive despite the Democratic tilt in current pricing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4454, "margin": -0.75}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6234, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.6548, "margin": 2.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6308, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.5679, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6942, "margin": 3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6077, "margin": 1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.6479, "margin": 2.0}]}